---
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of use"
  description={`The terms for using ${SITE.name}'s electricity prices and calculators.`}
  crumbs={[['Terms of use', '/terms/']]}
>
  <h1>Terms of use</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated October 29, 2026.</p>
  <p>
    By using {SITE.name} you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Estimates, not advice</h2>
  <p>
    The prices, bills and running costs on this site are estimates built from public averages and
    the numbers you enter. Your utility's rates, fees and taxes can differ, so your own bill is the
    final word. Nothing here is financial, legal or engineering advice. Check with your utility or a
    qualified professional before you make a decision that costs money, such as replacing a heating
    system.
  </p>

  <h2>Where the numbers come from</h2>
  <p>
    Energy prices come from the U.S. Energy Information Administration and are refreshed when it
    publishes new figures. Recent months are preliminary and may be revised. How each number is used
    is described on <a href="/methodology/">Data &amp; methodology</a>. We try to keep it accurate,
    but we cannot promise the data is complete, current or free of errors.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided as it is, without warranties of any kind. To the extent the law allows, we
    are not liable for any loss or damage that comes from using it or relying on its estimates.
  </p>

  <h2>Using our content</h2>
  <p>
    EIA data is public. The text, calculators and charts on this site are ours. You may quote or
    cite a figure or a short passage with a link back to the page it came from. Please do not copy
    whole pages or scrape the site in bulk.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    We link to other websites for reference. We do not control them and are not responsible for
    them.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    What we collect, and what we don't, is on the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The date at the top of this page shows the latest version, and
    continuing to use the site means you accept it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>
  </p>
</Base>
